# Patch: optimizer instances (GLOBAL_DP) for ZeRO-1 Muon (part of the muon-zero1 set)
#
# Problem:   the layer-wise + DistributedOptimizer split path (shard-aligned layout, patch 0001)
#            asserts num_distributed_optimizer_instances == 1 (instance id hard-coded to 0), and
#            LayerWiseDistributedOptimizer rejects instances altogether. Simulated inter-datacenter
#            training (launch.sh GLOBAL_DP) needs them.
# What:      factory: instance id from the inter-instance group, passed to the DistOpt (non-Muon)
#            sub-optimizer and to LayerWise, plus the intra-instance group for gradient statistics.
#            LayerWise with the shard-aligned layout: shard / all-gather over the intra-instance
#            dense and expert groups (each instance owns whole matrices over its ranks; DDP
#            reduce-scatters inside the instance and all-reduces the shards across instances);
#            grad norm / zero count / group checks reduced over the instance's ranks (a global
#            reduction would count every matrix once per instance); optimizer-state replica_id
#            carries the instance id so only instance 0 writes it. Legacy layout still refuses.
# Porting:   _get_megatron_emerging_optimizer in megatron/core/optimizer/__init__.py and
#            LayerWiseDistributedOptimizer.__init__/get_grad_norm/_get_grad_norm_for_group/
#            count_zeros/has_grad_norm_group/sharded_state_dict.
#
